<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">League of Lezhë</h1><p class="st-meta">1444 CE – 1479 CE · capital Krujë</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Alliance of Albanian lords under Skanderbeg that resisted the Ottoman Empire for a quarter of a century and became a symbol of Albanian unity.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 2 March 1444, in the Venetian-held town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lezhe">Lezhë</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a> gathered the leading Albanian nobles, among them the Arianiti, Dukagjini, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muzaka-family">Muzaka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thopia-family">Thopia</a>, Zaharia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balsic-noble-family">Balšić</a> families and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-crnojevic">Stefan Crnojević</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeta-region">Zeta</a>. They agreed to pool troops and revenues under his command against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kruje">Krujë</a> as the centre of resistance.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The league was a military alliance rather than a unified state: each lord kept his own lands, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a> led a mobile army that used mountain terrain to defeat larger Ottoman forces, as at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-torvioll">Torvioll</a> in 1444 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-albulena">Albulena</a> in 1457. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kruje">Krujë</a> withstood Ottoman sieges in 1450, 1466 and 1467. Skanderbeg sought support from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The alliance frayed early, through a war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1447 and defections of lords. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a> died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lezhe">Lezhë</a> in 1468, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leke-dukagjini">Lekë Dukagjini</a> and Venice fought on, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kruje">Krujë</a> fell in 1478 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shkoder">Shkodër</a> in 1479. Skanderbeg's flag and memory became central to Albanian nationalism.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/league-of-lezhe.jpg" alt="League of Lezhë" width="320" height="610"><figcaption>Image: Ahmet Q. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:League_of_Lezh%C3%AB,_1448-1468.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1444 CE – 1479 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Krujë</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Skanderbeg, Lekë Dukagjini</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Albanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/albania">Albania</a>, <a href="/countries/montenegro">Montenegro</a>, <a href="/countries/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>League of Alessio, Albanian League</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1462&amp;focus=league-of-lezhe" aria-label="League of Lezhë on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5158 689 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where League of Lezhë lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5478 945L5483 954M5478 945L5478 945M5478 945L5349 976M5478 945L5709 970"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5483 954h0M5478 945h0M5349 976h0M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5478 945h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5478 945h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1462&amp;focus=league-of-lezhe">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
